# The bird does not gain an attack -- it is replaced. The client keeps this
# skill's whole animation set under a `summon` node, and the 6th job skill that
# reads it says "while Fury of the Wild is summoned", so for forty seconds the
# Phoenix or the Frostprey IS this.
#
# 3.42 seconds is not published anywhere. It is twice the 1.71 the two birds
# are held at, which is what their animations say: theirs runs 1170ms and this
# one 2310ms, near enough exactly double. `attackAfter` is not the period --
# both birds state 450 against a real 1710.
#
# Reach is GMS's 10 and stays there: the summon's attack box is 730x240, and
# floor(730/70) is 10 on the nose.
#
# Damage is GMS's 450 + 15x, seven lines: 465% at level 1 and 900% at 30. A
# pulse on its own clock gets no Final Attack and no Shadow Partner, the rule
# every summon here follows -- nothing the character did not swing is doubled.
#
# Every explorer archer holds a bird by their third book, so GMS's "only while
# one is summoned" needs no gate.
name: "Fury of the Wild"
description:
  "Fills your summoned bird with an older, wilder power, and for a while it "
  "hunts as the thing it used to be."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 1 }
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN_V skill_order: 1 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_ARCHETYPE
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 119.5
cooldown_seconds_per_level: -0.5
buff {
  duration_seconds: 40.0
  pulse {
    label: "Empowered Summon"
    cast_interval_seconds: 3.42
    max_enemies: 10
    lines: 7
    base { skill_pct: 4.65 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.15 }
  }
}
